# Cloudflare Pages serves static assets with `max-age=14400` by default,
# so a browser that loaded app.js once would not ask for it again for
# four hours -- which is why a deploy did not show up until the cache was
# cleared. The HTML was already `max-age=0`, which is the trap: the page
# was new, the code behind it was not.
#
# The filenames here are not content-hashed (there is no build step, the
# modules are served as written), so the only safe cache is a
# revalidating one. `no-cache` does not mean "do not store" -- the
# browser keeps the file and asks the edge whether it changed, and the
# answer is a 304 with no body. The whole frontend is ~30 KB, and
# Cloudflare answers the revalidation from its own edge, so this costs a
# round trip, not a download.
#
# If a build step with hashed filenames ever lands, flip the hashed
# assets to `max-age=31536000, immutable` and leave the HTML revalidating.
#
# EVERY RULE HERE IS AN EXACT PATH, and it has to stay that way. The first
# version of this file used `/*.js` and `/*.css`, which `wrangler pages
# dev` parses and applies -- and which the production edge silently
# ignores. It deployed clean and changed nothing: the assets still came
# back `max-age=14400`. A splat appears to need to be the last thing in
# the pattern, so a mid-pattern one matches nothing and reports no error.
# Do not reintroduce one without checking the LIVE headers afterwards.
#
# A blanket `/*` would work, but `_headers` APPENDS to what a Pages
# Function already sent, so it would make /api/* come back
# `Cache-Control: no-cache, no-store`. The API's own `no-store` in
# lib/http.ts is the stronger and correct answer for a private roster of
# real names and bib numbers, and exact paths leave it alone.
#
# Adding a module to public/? Add it here too. `npm run deploy` checks
# this list against the directory and refuses to deploy if one is missing,
# so the mistake cannot reach production silently -- which is exactly how
# the splat version got there.
#
/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/me
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/app.css
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/app.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/browse.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/form.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/gate.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/me.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/version.json
  Cache-Control: no-cache
